# Backtest exports + local DBs — never commit (huge, and licensed data must not be redistributed)
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored `data/` also matches `valuation/data/`,
# which is APPLICATION SOURCE: on 2026-08-07 a new module there (`valuation/data/beta.py`) was
# silently unaddable, and since `wacc.py` imports it lazily it would have shipped as a runtime
# ModuleNotFoundError on exactly the path it was written for. The six older files in that
# package survive only because git ignore rules do not apply to already-tracked files.
# The licensed Sharadar exports live in the repo-root `data/` and stay fully ignored; `*.db`,
# `*.zip` and `*.csv.gz` below remain path-independent guards.
/data/
*.db
# Raw vendor bulk downloads. data/ already covers data/raw/, but these are multi-hundred-MB
# licensed archives, so this is a second, path-independent guard: a zip anywhere in the tree
# is never committable, however it got there.
*.zip
*.csv.gz
*.parquet

# C6 (2026-08-07): `quant_data/` at the repo root is a loose EXTRACTED copy of the
# bot state (24 files, byte-identical to `options-bot/quant_data.tgz` — measured,
# not assumed). It was untracked AND unignored, so `git add -A` in the primary
# checkout would have committed bot runtime state into the Valquo repo. Ignored
# here as a guard; the copy itself is redundant and slated for deletion.
/quant_data/

# C6 (2026-08-07): `options-bot2/` is a SECOND, older copy of the whole bot tree
# sitting inside the repo folder (~285 KB of duplicated source plus its own
# quant_data.tgz). It is not tracked and, until now, was not ignored either — so
# it showed up as untracked in the primary checkout and a single `git add -A`
# would have committed a duplicate of the bot codebase at a stale revision.
# It is kept on disk deliberately (it is a third independent copy of the
# recovered `options/data/*.py`), so ignore it rather than deleting it.
options-bot2/

# O8: full VRP equity curves + trade logs are derived data (~5 MB), regenerable
options-bot/options_backtest/options_backtest_*.json
options-bot/screener/.cache/
options-bot/screener/prefetch.*
options-bot/screener/insider.*
options-bot/quant_bots/c5_ingest.*

# Internal business/launch planning - untracked 2026-08-16 when the repo went public.
# These name a separate LLC, entity structuring and securities-law posture, and are
# not project documentation. They remain on disk. NOTE: they are still present in
# public git HISTORY - see HANDOFF_ci.md for the full remediation options.
LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md
GO_LIVE.md
